# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        url: "https://financialdata.net/documentation"
      }
      description: "This API provides access to a wide range of financial data including market data, company fundamentals, and alternative data. Users can make requests to retrieve stock symbols, prices, company information, ESG scores and ratings, mutual fund holdings, and more. The data covers thousands of securities including stocks, ETFs, funds, and commodities."
      servers: [
        {
          description: "Production server"
          url: "https://financialdata.net/api/v1"
        }
      ]
      title: "Financial Data API"
      version: "1.0.0"
      tagline: "Stock, ETF, crypto, forex, options, futures and fundamentals across US and international markets from a single REST API"
      homepage: "https://financialdata.net"
      docs_url: "https://financialdata.net/documentation"
      license_short: "Tiered subscription (Free, Standard, Premium); API key required."
      license_md: `- Operated commercially by financialdata.net with Free, Standard and Premium tiers
- Requires an API key, passed as a \`key\` query parameter on every request
- Pricing, redistribution rules and per-tier quotas are governed by the financialdata.net terms of service
- CORS is disabled, so requests should be made from a backend rather than directly from a browser`
      about_md: `[Financial Data API](https://financialdata.net) is a commercial REST service that aggregates market data, company fundamentals and alternative datasets for equities, ETFs, mutual funds, options, futures, cryptocurrencies and forex pairs. It covers both US-listed and international securities through a single endpoint surface at \`https://financialdata.net/api/v1\`.

What you get from the API:

- Symbol catalogues for stocks, international stocks, ETFs, commodities, OTC, indexes, options, futures, crypto and forex
- Real-time and historical quotes and prices, including minute bars for stocks, crypto and forex
- Company basics, key metrics, market cap, employee counts, executive compensation and securities information
- Income statements, balance sheets and cash flow statements for US and international issuers
- Financial ratios across liquidity, solvency, efficiency, profitability and valuation
- Option chains with Greeks, plus futures prices
- Event calendars (earnings, IPOs, dividends), press releases and SEC/Fed releases
- Insider trading, institutional holdings, ETF and mutual fund holdings, ESG scores and investment adviser records

Authentication is via an API key appended as \`?key=API_KEY\` (or \`&key=API_KEY\` when other parameters are present). Most list endpoints return 300-500 records per call and support an \`offset\` parameter for pagination. CORS is disabled on the service.`
      entity_desc: {
        basic_information: "Company-level reference data such as profile, key metrics, market cap, employee count and executive compensation."
        crypto_currency: "Cryptocurrency symbols, metadata, quotes and historical/minute prices."
        derivatives_data: "Option chains with prices and Greeks, plus futures symbols and prices."
        esg_data: "Environmental, social and governance ratings and scores for covered companies."
        etf_data: "ETF reference data, prices and holdings."
        event_calendar: "Forward-looking calendars for earnings, IPOs and dividends."
        financial_ratio: "Computed liquidity, solvency, efficiency, profitability and valuation ratios per issuer."
        financial_statement: "Income statements, balance sheets and cash flow statements for US and international companies."
        forex_data: "Currency pair symbols, quotes and historical/minute prices."
        insider_trading: "Reported insider transactions for covered securities."
        institutional_trading: "Institutional holdings and position changes for covered securities."
        investment_adviser: "Reference records for registered investment advisers."
        market_data: "Real-time and historical quotes, latest prices, minute bars and volumes across stocks, OTC and commodities."
        market_index: "Index symbols, quotes, historical prices and constituent membership."
        market_new: "Press releases plus SEC and Federal Reserve releases relevant to covered issuers."
        miscellaneous_data: "Supplementary datasets that do not fall into the other entity groups."
        mutual_fund: "Mutual fund reference data, prices and holdings."
        symbol_list: "Master symbol catalogues for stocks, international stocks, ETFs, commodities and OTC securities."
      }
      auth: false
    }
  }
}
